        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "On \\( [0,2\\pi] \\), the inequality \\( \\sin x\\geq\\cos 2x \\) is satisfied for which set of values of \\(x\\)?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Using \\(\\cos 2x=1-2\\sin^2x\\), the inequality becomes \\(2\\sin^2x+\\sin x-1\\geq0\\), or \\((2\\sin x-1)(\\sin x+1)\\geq0\\). Hence \\(\\sin x\\geq\\frac12\\) or \\(\\sin x=-1\\), giving the stated set.",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 66,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
            "subject": "Mathematics",
            "creatorId": null,
            "classLevel": "Class 12",
